## Source Comparison

The original has four full-width rows. Its upper block is 2 rows x 5 columns including the heading column, and its lower block is 2 rows x 6 columns including the heading column. Both share the same outer width, with distinct internal column divisions. The middle boundary consists of two separate full-width horizontal lines.

The modern preview preserves all nine name/value pairs in their source cells:

| Block | Source Column Including Heading | Body | Source Mass (kg) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Upper | 2 | Mercury | 3.17 * 10^23 |
| Upper | 3 | Venus | 4.87 * 10^24 |
| Upper | 4 | Earth | 5.98 * 10^24 |
| Upper | 5 | Mars | 6.40 * 10^23 |
| Lower | 2 | Jupiter | 1.90 * 10^27 |
| Lower | 3 | Saturn | 5.69 * 10^26 |
| Lower | 4 | Uranus | 8.70 * 10^25 |
| Lower | 5 | Neptune | 1.03 * 10^26 |
| Lower | 6 | Pluto | 5.40 * 10^24 |

All nine coefficients and exponents match the source. The four terminal zeros and the internal zero in 1.03 remain visible. No mass was substituted with a current astronomical estimate.

## Native-Width Visual Gate

At the inspected 640 x 320 size, all 22 labels are visible: nine names, nine scientific-notation values, and four heading/unit labels. English `Body` and `Mass (kg)` appear in both blocks. The upper block has five columns and the lower block has six. The six-pixel middle gap visibly separates the two horizontal rules, and the side joins keep one connected frame.

No label touches a cell divider or another label. The longest labels and scientific notation fit their cells. No clipping or missing border, cell, name, digit, exponent, or unit is apparent. The renderer report declares an actual-width minimum of 16 px, with no collisions or display failures; the preview supports its readability and containment findings.

Clean linework, equal-width cells within each block, English headings, and superscript notation are modern presentation decisions. They do not change source data or membership. No Chinese/Cyrillic source labeling, cultural ornament, archival texture, sorted answer list, or computed ratio is visible.

## Current Question

Current exercise 181a asks for the nine bodies in the table to be written in increasing mass order. The figure includes all nine, including Pluto, and its `Body` heading does not classify all nine as planets. Exercise 181b asks for a Jupiter/Earth mass ratio; the source values needed for that task are present but no ratio result is supplied.

The immutable FIRST spec still contains the former 181a wording. That is a known text-binding issue only, not a source or visual defect. Current formal binding must use the authorized affected1 spec/render after static equivalence succeeds.

## Substantive Decision

PASS for source fidelity, current-question suitability, and the one inspected native-640 FIRST visual. No geometry repair or further image view is required. Formal review is a separate action, conditional on successful static current-binding reconciliation; this observation file is not a `ld-s10y-image/review@1` record and does not authorize promotion.
